{{also|rundown|run-down}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|run<,,ran,run> down}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To hit someone with a car or other vehicle and injure or kill them.
#: {{ux|en|He was '''run down''' while crossing the main road.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[criticize]] someone or an organisation, often [[unfairly]].
#: {{ux|en|Whatever the company says, the media is going to '''run''' them '''down'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|My sister is always '''running''' me '''down''' in front of my friends.}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't '''run''' yourself '''down''' so much!}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1777|author=w:Richard Brinsley Sheridan|title=The School for Scandal|section=I.i
|passage=Ha! ha! ha! 'tis very hard for them to leave a subject they have not quite '''run down'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|find after a long search}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[find]] something or someone after [[search]]ing for a [[long]] time.
#: {{syn|en|run to earth#Verb|run to ground#Verb}}
#: {{cot|en|run in#English:_arrest or especially track down and arrest}}
#: {{ux|en|I finally managed to '''run down''' that report. I had filed it incorrectly.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To lose [[power]] slowly. Used for a [[machine]], [[battery]], or other powered device.
#: {{ux|en|You need to wind up the clock every day so that it doesn't '''run down'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|If you don't switch off the car lights, you will '''run''' the battery '''down'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To read quickly a list or other short text.
#: {{ux|en|'''Running down''' the list of suggestions, I can see three we can discard immediately.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To describe in the form of a [[rundown]], a rough outline or summary.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Nora Roberts|title=The Name of the Game
|passage=When the minute was up, John Jay managed to make the woman twice as nervous as he '''ran down''' the rules and the possibilities.}}
# {{lb|en|British|transitive}} To [[reduce]] the size or [[stock]] levels of a business, often with a view to [[closure]].
#: {{ux|en|The board of directors have decided to '''run down''' the stocks held in storage prior to offering the company for sale.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 November 30|author=Nigel Harris|title=A bid to break the other side?|journal=RAIL|issue=971|page=3|text=Social media has been full of strident criticism of a Government perceived as pursuing a conscious policy to '''run down''' - even destroy - our railway.}}
# To decline in quality or condition.
#: {{ux|en|to '''run down''' in health}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 26|author=Paul Clifton|title="Intolerable" service cuts under emergency COVID timetables|journal=RAIL|issue=949|page=8|text=TravelWatch SouthWest Chairman Chris Irwin said: "This is intolerable. The South West deserves levelling up, not '''running down'''. SWR and its sponsors in the Department of Transport must be called to account."}}
# {{lb|en|hunting}} To [[chase]] till the object pursued is [[capture]]d or [[exhausted]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''run down''' a stag}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|transitive}} To run against and [[sink]], as a vessel.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1943|month=May and June|author=Chas. S. Lake|title=Some Continental Travel Experiences (1922-1939)—III|journal=Railway Magazine|page=143|text=The ''Jylland'' only missed '''running down''' a schooner by a few yards in the fog; it was a near thing—near enough, in fact, to allow of some shouted remarks between those on the bridge of the motorship and the man at the wheel of the schooner to be clearly heard.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=Guadalcanal Campaign - The Big Night Battle: Night 1 (IJN 3(?) : 2 USN)|date=10 March 2021|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221017005233/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archivedate=17 October 2022|accessdate=6 November 2022|time=14:35|text=''Hiei'' now loomed into the action, causing the leading U.S. destroyers to scatter before the oncoming behemoth lest they be '''run down'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[crush]]; to [[overthrow]]; to [[overbear]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1736|author=w:George Berkeley|title=A Discourse addressed to Magistrates and Men of Authority
|passage=Religion is {{...}}'''run down''' by the prevailing licence of these times.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|AAVE}} To approach (someone, thing or place) aggressively, as to attack.
#: ''He '''ran down''' on Rashad and them.''

====Usage notes====
* In all transitive senses except that of “to read quickly”, the object can come before or after the particle. If the object is a pronoun, then it must come before the particle.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|hit with a vehicle}} {{l|en|run over}}, {{l|en|knock down}}
* {{sense|criticise}} {{l|en|put down}}, {{l|en|demean}}, {{l|en|berate}}
* {{sense|locate}} {{l|en|track down}}

